# Every file in this project is written with LF line endings and the whole
# verification workflow for it is byte-level (md5-matched copies in
# pre-fix-files/, diff-vs-backup before and after each edit). The Git build on
# this machine turns core.autocrlf on in its system config, which would rewrite
# the working copy to CRLF the next time Git checks files out and make every
# future diff - and every hash comparison - show all churn. Turning conversion
# off keeps the bytes in the repository identical to the bytes Apache serves.
* -text
